Spring Boot scans the classpath and applies relevant auto-configurations using the `spring.factories` file located in the `META-INF` directory of each Spring Boot starter. These auto-configurations are implemented as `@Configuration` classes.

## `@EnableAutoConfiguration`

This annotation tells Spring Boot to enable auto-configuration based on the dependencies on the classpath. The context shows it as one of the annotations that make up `@SpringBootApplication`, alongside:

- `@Configuration`: marks the class as a source of bean definitions
- `@ComponentScan`: scans for components (`@Component`, `@Service`, `@Repository`, `@Controller`) in the current package and subpackages

